 ],
 "portSitesAtHead": {
  "turnStartEncore": "src/engine/factoryBattleScriptFullTurnDecision.ts:3151-3155 playerRetargets / trainerRetargets = actionRetargetsAtExecution(rules.rulesContext, ...) (function :1628-1636) read the TURN-START rules context; the move id / slot come from actionMoveId (:2416-2442) on the same turn-start context (lockedMoveDecision :2366-2395 only auto-confirms an Encore that already existed at selection)",
  "actionTimeCheck": "src/engine/factoryBattleScriptFullTurnDecision.ts:1677-1690 runMoveAction re-evaluates only the :130-134 arm (actionTakesChosenMoveChangedArm :1666-1675) on priorState.rulesContext; for action 2 (call site :3012-3022, second.moveId / second.moveSlot / second.retargetsAtExecution) an Encore written by action 1's trysetencore is never consulted",
  "whatThePortRuns": "turn 2: the banked TACKLE with its full hit chain (accuracycheck where the ROM draws BattleTurnPassed) -- first divergence turn 2 index 2"
 },
 "fixShape": "In runMoveAction (factoryBattleScriptFullTurnDecision.ts:1677), before the :130-134 check, evaluate HandleAction_UseMove's Encore arms on the ACTION-TIME battler (priorState.rulesContext.battlers[mover]): (a) battle_util.c:111-117 encoredMove != 0 && moves[encoredMovePos] == encoredMove -> executed move = encoredMove, move slot (gCurrMovePos / chosenMovePositions, PP deduction) = encoredMovePos, retarget via drawActionMoveTarget; (b) :119-128 encoredMove != 0 && moves[encoredMovePos] != encoredMove -> clear Encore, run moves[encoredMovePos], retarget. Only when neither fires fall through to :130-134 / plain. This subsumes the turn-start retargetsAtExecution for Encore (action 1 sees the same state either way). Post-fix sequence = the ROM's (turn 2: acc, Encore timer, GetMoveTarget, acc, crit, dmg, SEWC, BTP).",
